  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Midwifery Capacity Advancement for Equitable Sexual and Reproductive Health and Reproductive Rights (MARCH) Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The funding is for UNFPA to provide technical assistance on three interconnected pillars of midwifery capacity advancement for sexual and reproductive health and rights: regulatory frameworks, midwifery education, and continuing professional development. 

This project is aimed at improving national capacities to implement a regulatory framework that enhances the quality of midwifery workforce with the following outcomes. 
the following outcomes. 
1. Regulatory framework at the national level effectively provides a national strategy for continuing professional development of the midwifery workforce
Under this outcome, the project will develop policy recommendations, a a National Midwifery Continuing Professional Development (CPD) Framework, and a CPD pilot programme to improve the quality of midwifery services. 
2. Midwifery education stakeholders are enhanced through the implementation of midwifery education that is aligned to International Confederation of Midwives (ICM) standards.
Under this outcome, the project will improve the accreditation standards for midwifery education aligned with the ICM through some stages from baseline assessment of the current accreditation to piloting the upgraded accreditations in selected midwifery institutions (health polytechnics). It will then train the midwifery teachers with updated teaching methodologies and resources based on the new curricula. 
3. Midwifery Continuing Professional Development (CPD) programmes are strengthened in producing empowered and competent health workers who are capable of providing quality reproductive, maternal, newborn, child and adolescent health services.
Under this outcome, the project will build professional capacity of in-service midwifery, as well as other skills such as conducting research/study on midwifery-led Care (MLC).</narrative>
  </description>
